WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.088
Step three lists what didn't
run, with its reason.

2
00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:05.762
One test is planned, under construction.

3
00:00:05.762 --> 00:00:11.252
The six skips carry five different reasons:
not licensed for workload I D, two not

4
00:00:11.252 --> 00:00:16.825
applicable, not connected to a service, a
timeout, and no compatible license found.

5
00:00:16.825 --> 00:00:22.025
Step four sorts those reasons with the
kit's own function, convert to Z T A result.

6
00:00:22.025 --> 00:00:24.663
Not licensed becomes skipped, licensing.

7
00:00:24.663 --> 00:00:27.500
Not connected becomes
skipped, disconnected.

8
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.462
Not applicable stays
skipped, not applicable.

9
00:00:30.462 --> 00:00:33.162
The timeout becomes unable to evaluate.

10
00:00:33.162 --> 00:00:35.676
And an investigate result becomes fail.

11
00:00:35.676 --> 00:00:39.712
So that's four skips, four different
meanings, and none of them a failure.

12
00:00:39.712 --> 00:00:43.759
The investigate result is a
finding until someone reviews it,

13
00:00:43.759 --> 00:00:45.425
which you'll do in Module 3.

14
00:00:45.425 --> 00:00:49.800
The page lists every command for
the lab in order, ready to paste.
